From 53fe89336c924e3faa191e127a61a99bac0e7518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sellwane7 <sellwanemosia708@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 09:07:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Trading page blank-screen crash, live indicator color,
 add navbar date + user
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add ErrorBoundary around routed pages: without one, any render-time
  throw unmounted the whole app (navbar included) to a blank black
  screen. Now a crash stays contained to the page and shows the real
  error instead of failing silently.
- Harden OrderBook.jsx and useOrderBookSocket.js against bids/asks
  ever being null/undefined instead of an array — the likely trigger
  for the blank Trading page, since [...asks] throws synchronously
  during render with no guard.
- Change the order book '.live' status color from amber to a
  dedicated --success green, without touching the shared --accent
  variable used elsewhere in the UI.
- Add a live date readout to the navbar.
- Add a logged-in user indicator (person icon + email) to the navbar.
  authStore now persists the email that /api/auth/login and
  /register already return but the frontend was discarding.
